#. Context: Help › explanation of the Graham Number. Use the local decimal
#. separator in 22.5.
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:103
msgid ""
"√(22.5 × EPS × book value per share) — Benjamin Graham's classic value "
"formula. Needs positive trailing earnings and book value per share."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › fair-value model name, exactly as in the legal
#. Methodology document § 3: earnings per share × a sector P/E multiple
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:106
msgid "Price/earnings value"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › explanation of the P/E fair value model
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:106
msgid "Trailing EPS × a sector-typical fair P/E multiple."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › fair-value model name, exactly as in the legal
#. Methodology document § 3
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:107
msgid "Earnings power value (EPV)"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › explanation of EPV
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:107
msgid ""
"Normalised earnings capitalised at the cost of capital, deliberately "
"ignoring speculative growth."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › fair-value model name, exactly as in the legal
#. Methodology document § 3
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:109
msgid "Dividend model, single stage"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › explanation of the one-stage DDM
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:109
msgid ""
"Gordon growth model: next year's expected dividend discounted at (cost of"
" equity − perpetual growth rate). Only applies to dividend payers."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › fair-value model name, exactly as in the legal
#. Methodology document § 3
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:111
msgid "Dividend model, multi-stage"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › explanation of the two-stage DDM
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:111
msgid ""
"A higher-growth phase followed by a stable terminal-growth phase, each "
"discounted back separately. Also dividend-payer only."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › description of the book value (fallback) model
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:113
msgid ""
"Book value per share × the sector's median price/book ratio. Used only when "
"Graham, P/E and EPV all fail, typically for a loss-maker."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › fair-value model name, exactly as in the legal
#. Methodology document § 3
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:115
msgid "Free cash flow value (fallback)"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Methodology › description of the free cash flow value (fallback)
#. model
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:115
msgid ""
"Free cash flow × a fixed multiple, minus net debt, per share. Used only when "
"Graham, P/E and EPV all fail."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › FAQ question
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:122
msgid "How is the composite fair value calculated?"
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:123
msgid ""
"Each stock is valued by every model that applies to it. Their values are "
"combined into one weighted fair value, capped when a single model runs far above"
" the others. Margin of safety is the discount of the price to that figure. Both "
"are model estimates."
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:126
msgid "What does the weighted composite score mean?"
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:127
msgid ""
"A 0–100 value-weighted mean of the model scores across your holdings. It "
"describes the portfolio; it is not a recommendation. A holding that fails a "
"quality screen counts with its score of 0; a holding without a score (No signal)"
" is left out."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › FAQ question
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:130 uvalu/pages_/help.py:144
msgid "How often do prices update?"
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:131
msgid ""
"During the free beta prices are delayed quotes from Yahoo Finance; each signal "
"shows the time of the price it used. Fundamentals are refreshed about every 24 "
"hours. Real-time prices are not offered."
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:134
msgid "Why does a stock show “Screened out”?"
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:135
msgid ""
"It breaks one of the quality rules listed on this page; the explanation next to "
"the badge names which. Its composite score is set to 0. It still appears in your"
" portfolio and valuations."
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › FAQ question
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:138 uvalu/pages_/help.py:148
msgid "Which exchanges are covered?"
msgstr ""

#. Context: Help › FAQ answer. Exchange names are proper names; only translate
#. city names if usual.
#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:139
msgid "Euronext Amsterdam/Brussels/Paris, XETRA, SIX Swiss, and Borsa Italiana."
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:145
msgid ""
"The demo shows end-of-day closing prices, refreshed each weekday evening; the "
"provider is named under Data sources. The fundamentals come from the companies' "
"annual reports and are updated once a year. Intraday prices are not shown."
msgstr ""

#: uvalu/pages_/help.py:149
msgid ""
"The demo covers 9 stocks on Euronext Amsterdam, Brussels and Paris, Xetra, SIX "
"Swiss Exchange, Nasdaq Copenhagen and the London Stock Exchange, plus one ETF."
msgstr ""

